{"title":"2026 Bespoked Osaka Picks 04: Crumbworks, Morralito, Prova, Sim Works, Stayer – John Watson","link":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-05","date":1793255400000,"content":"<p><em>Maido from Osaka! Cari and John were in attendance at the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/2026-bespoked-osaka\" target=\"_blank\">2026 Bespoked Osaka</a> event, where they documented a variety of bikes from the global framebuilding community. Read on for a look at the Bespoked Osaka venue and a selection of builders including Crumbworks, Morralito, Prova, Sim Works, and Stayer…</em><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/674bbda45b81ccf146e5921a7d1730f35f7fa225fc72c7acbb87d87063cdd108.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/aebde258c15f14b09bce726406ab68a56703887b03426761a44c16f795188250.jpg 640w, /media/674bbda45b81ccf146e5921a7d1730f35f7fa225fc72c7acbb87d87063cdd108.jpg 1800w, /media/e1cb4e2df6894b6ae66b33ae30c90e0c6f7168c050285b4fe75cab0a6e89f9a1.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.crumbworks.jp/en\" target=\"_blank\">Crumbworks</a> x <a href=\"https://www.faretsbicycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Farets Bicycles</a> (Big) Chunk</h3>\n<p>Tokyo-based Crumbworks had a wonderful display at the 2026 Bespoked Osaka showcase featuring a crowd favorite, the Chunk, front and center. The Chunk is made by Farets Bicycles, Crumbworks’ in-house frame company. Owner Keita Matsumoto’s vision for the brand is inspired by vintage cruisers, brands like Crust, and Rivendell. The Chunk is a rigid MTB with clearance for 26 x 2.8″, 27.5 x 2.8″, or 700 x 50 mm tires and lots of standover.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4206c8cb297936e46075f9346cdb13f97f2f3a3957a3fc64936baff9057bd748.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/71385da9084af431bae8cd2577cb7f2402e8468976a0e50bdaebe40d0ea183d2.jpg 800w, /media/4206c8cb297936e46075f9346cdb13f97f2f3a3957a3fc64936baff9057bd748.jpg 1600w, /media/2d1af41da85bf1245f269406fd54db1d39a9ba942135b288541c79aa56d9b43e.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a6464444a8026c20c3e78de4a4e9b66c5261c4f96b492162db4dee1852b5f77a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/6fe1e862f97f708cdfd7deb8a11205c16f5cafd99f71ce37bba76e9bef0d16b2.jpg 800w, /media/a6464444a8026c20c3e78de4a4e9b66c5261c4f96b492162db4dee1852b5f77a.jpg 1600w, /media/2e32298107cabcc540d0fd7a38dcc417c1cdfddf99496281532468c057677809.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d6cea725d7363436a07ea4e759d400a17d45f7a8011a9868f8f6b9856b5b567a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/90ef1c2c6af8460a47051ae658a0f8c437e031c8b10f3b4cdf042175a5fadae8.jpg 800w, /media/d6cea725d7363436a07ea4e759d400a17d45f7a8011a9868f8f6b9856b5b567a.jpg 1600w, /media/d7bae1d93619e3a5800c2e43ae24ba06d35d3cd08f0e008e51750f006f97bf79.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Its tall stack and segmented fork are perhaps overshadowed by the swooping top tube and step-through frame, which still provides enough room for a framebag. The Chunk uses a 1″ steerer, designed for quill stems, allowing for handlebar flex in all the right ways.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/24cffed8f18a4fd7810c46bca25fc5a6ab60508d9394a112894230a136165ba9.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ba34e1fea576f8333bffaa5fe06edd4192616da43229cf26ef8ab607cbd1bad7.jpg 640w, /media/24cffed8f18a4fd7810c46bca25fc5a6ab60508d9394a112894230a136165ba9.jpg 1800w, /media/2f9f621078a52cad8123fa7299c7126b53b09296cea1af39a61a91cab1b8c26f.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Zenzay, the designer of the Chunk and its headbadge was kind enough to pose with his bike, which was a standout at the show. Fitted with custom <a href=\"https://www.huuungry.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">Hungry bags</a>, they really tie the room together.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/193a241d500463267ba828d2a24ee934757cebbb407fc46540a3f74967acbef7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/bbc53fbc5abbb55e4880992be4bc501d66e3b2fc73c226366c56c5ff867c4bb4.jpg 640w, /media/193a241d500463267ba828d2a24ee934757cebbb407fc46540a3f74967acbef7.jpg 1800w, /media/fbc5f6272071369db35427570c8a3087980825811aa9e7100007f62415ad8be4.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.crumbworks.jp/en\" target=\"_blank\">Crumbworks</a> Mini Chunk</h3>\n<p>Teaming up with legendary Japanese builder Osamu Fukuda, who runs Raizin Works, Crumbworks designed a mini velo version of the Chunk, dubbed the Mini Chunk. Designer Zenzay worked closely with Fukuda to ensure the lines and stance of the Mini Chunk were in line with the Big Chunk.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/25971442bbd1f96c654831821d202199cb25286a2cbfde4e71d6a58b029ab791.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0a79e0517e2f633b638a8580ed18bd03e85be1d3df35b7b2df40f123dfaa2a62.jpg 800w, /media/25971442bbd1f96c654831821d202199cb25286a2cbfde4e71d6a58b029ab791.jpg 1600w, /media/1c54cfbe1bb8d81904c00861d1faaf0530d91fb2e6853d9a37c377b69c221d9a.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f4e1d9c8114a56e7c70cca6ede603d555cb638d4b7cb9a507093988f571279c8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0bbdf9400cd0eb939b0d9f69456bcd0afdbf42cb8dfc5d77f653ced5fd1157ec.jpg 800w, /media/f4e1d9c8114a56e7c70cca6ede603d555cb638d4b7cb9a507093988f571279c8.jpg 1600w, /media/082ed529c62c41ccfa4a8e74821ed84af0aac460e82174e28d6b21b4ad30d424.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/6881385d913d791e89c2a72490805f71d73af2aaeabf968d77c6c6f15e2c9046.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/6eeeaf2a2299479f795b24db670deafaadcc736653631f9ef65446a033b8bbd0.jpg 800w, /media/6881385d913d791e89c2a72490805f71d73af2aaeabf968d77c6c6f15e2c9046.jpg 1600w, /media/87e1c03572b00d4ad6cadb43127d458e0b8e777f9a1725c1082e590bc32ba425.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>That includes plentiful tire clearance for a cushioned ride, a tall stack height for flat, swept-back Magic Components “<a href=\"https://www.crumbworks.jp/products/magic-components-kt-800-v2\" target=\"_blank\">KT-800</a>” bars. Fukuda’s fillet brazing is on full display with the Mini Chunk, while the (Big) Chunk is made in Taiwan through Crumbworks’ partners and is TIG-welded. Look out for the Mini Chunk in 2027 from Crumbworks!</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/38128fe1619d4ca1faa4eab0345d48cb6949d752edcc15a54a4b83daa479ea22.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/fd78dc5cd19908119e6c6cb0d4c95b25b44aeb0e2892f693c4143dfd29d9762f.jpg 800w, /media/38128fe1619d4ca1faa4eab0345d48cb6949d752edcc15a54a4b83daa479ea22.jpg 1600w, /media/3d8c4a4703cea3fcc8aac78b5035012ea711d0d570f4f5abedafd64cf618718e.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e26dc5fb9225223f15d88aa59cb58eecc439131ab1644dc70f3cba319b5944cf.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d1d1ee9ee42b77280a4f25b616a9d910d0737b559e65a7c6432ce8e33ddab02d.jpg 800w, /media/e26dc5fb9225223f15d88aa59cb58eecc439131ab1644dc70f3cba319b5944cf.jpg 1600w, /media/7cd72ecc4b50a20c3dff791dbe6f7b0ff54f3ba3c709053f5c364a992e082591.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/eff0e899cbe49c14a0c44749542dab64c797a75e964da69e7efa650869be43cd.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ae9c84f2ceace65d17da6c26a1701c19ea9190b5f639a826e649e0ff67b9a016.jpg 800w, /media/eff0e899cbe49c14a0c44749542dab64c797a75e964da69e7efa650869be43cd.jpg 1600w, /media/069520305a6029907fa961da17a0d1214d9c61ba77ec5310b3bad1e9c6e310b6.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Crumbworks owner Keita was there, displaying the new Babylnd Bikes collaboration, launched at Bespoked Osaka. These shirts are available in store at Crumbworks and on <a href=\"https://www.babyldn.com/merch-1/p/crumbworks-x-babyldn-long-sleeve-tee\" target=\"_blank\">Babyldn Bikes’ webshop</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/69726beb85918e062e442cb819af2423e1c568572eb673a8a2f254269927e699.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/806086afb8067cb73da9caa66dc41670583614a80684c23ab872ea22dfb21785.jpg 640w, /media/69726beb85918e062e442cb819af2423e1c568572eb673a8a2f254269927e699.jpg 1800w, /media/0206311933d23ad5ad40155759988d004ad8550355620c47eff730f73d960795.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Many thanks to Keita for the thorough explanation of the Crumbworks line and for the hangs!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/crumbworks.co/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@Crumbworks</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9fe9c3b8b0223f2280ee5ca832b6642065f0ac22a7e8a1a1642b005806d79be2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/cea32f5a602ab39087f64436a4fcc5e5129ee13c54533952c5cc01e172d8dbfd.jpg 640w, /media/9fe9c3b8b0223f2280ee5ca832b6642065f0ac22a7e8a1a1642b005806d79be2.jpg 1800w, /media/3538b95edeb173c0fe6a5fd0c3ebbd32fb40f9c77b8fa48b7c1298cf74516a2b.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.morralitobikes.com/inicio\" target=\"_blank\">Morralito</a> Inicio Cargo Bike</h3>\n<p>Mexico City-based Morralito is a collaborative effort between Mario Guzman, Elias Cattan, architects/designers, and Eli “De Bicla” Acosta, a framebuilder. We’ve <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/file-till-you-die-frame-builder-eli-de-bicla-acosta-from-basica-studio-in-mexico-city\" target=\"_blank\">featured Eli’s work before here on The Radavist</a> thanks to Dani and Karla. Morralito brought the Inicio, an adaptable cargo bike, designed and built for modern city living.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a6fc59030011b7b059feda2921f60aa0ff0c72e282afe0a9b628e9cc36603d84.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/17d401efa293bee3d461ce4d51979e3a47a25c9c71ee054b3868a2efbdc6763c.jpg 800w, /media/fcda9b5beae0be6a926f58ec7319ffb19fb41044bb47c7c1bd98af6020e6bd67.jpg 1600w, /media/a6fc59030011b7b059feda2921f60aa0ff0c72e282afe0a9b628e9cc36603d84.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d7178a6e7bcd3d27bcff0173a4534b4e1711d353f424680fc28b648cdc241620.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/048f8ff744e7ac6844653428a115ac248bb8169e9b29057479dc23c8940fd3bd.jpg 800w, /media/8d1b7bf279ca3d363a5ee3d4b1b66bf4fc6c448fdd8cbc612612601b96c9fd3c.jpg 1600w, /media/d7178a6e7bcd3d27bcff0173a4534b4e1711d353f424680fc28b648cdc241620.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>It’s a bike designed around 7 possible builds. You can build it fully mechanical, as shown, or remove the bottom bracket assemblage and install an electric drivetrain. The front box can be removed, and it can be run as a mini velo, or you can swap in a smaller box, a larger box, or you can run it in its long configuration as shown, or a more collapsible/stowable option.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4fb098989208f0c0656cb92bad2aacf0a552e94697fd4cf6349fded9e9a75c79.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d19e77e7682c65edb30bc4f7fca4ede1aad3b607a4ac0b6bcd3444f2bc47b04f.jpg 800w, /media/4fb098989208f0c0656cb92bad2aacf0a552e94697fd4cf6349fded9e9a75c79.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9658f0d3fcce2487dd38fe8a292e025874664ae4a66f50fccb940fea1ded21a3.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/47af51fc550f0538cdb867c5f30c24d00a433edd94e76871f6fa06c04275aafe.jpg 800w, /media/9658f0d3fcce2487dd38fe8a292e025874664ae4a66f50fccb940fea1ded21a3.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/c01c73848f834811ee96ed3c07e8c2422b08babe8e84f3d9a87663c6fb3d60b8.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/c4d1b4ea758fd4c2db9a5fc598b70594afc8291682c624dfdb190c524171ea6d.jpg 800w, /media/c01c73848f834811ee96ed3c07e8c2422b08babe8e84f3d9a87663c6fb3d60b8.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/deadf283d4400a972b30512afb91bea74984f828839752a9baab2a2518001c9c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/2a369f007bd85d4bfa87f281f4f67ec70c248bc45f80342dcb395273eee042e8.jpg 800w, /media/deadf283d4400a972b30512afb91bea74984f828839752a9baab2a2518001c9c.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The details and paint design reflect the landscape surrounding Mexico City, with large mountains, and are imbued with the bright, vibrant Mexican culture. When I was given the duty of awarding the best Utility Bike at the 2026 Bespoked Osaka showcase, this was the obvious winner.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b4e8faddcc050ddeacf97f9c664ea5a958df787c7310abc60562a7bb66c41a57.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/220327828895b5080e76cf3bca20d9005b0dfe5bfd19a522095e65a34ecbedb4.jpg 640w, /media/b4e8faddcc050ddeacf97f9c664ea5a958df787c7310abc60562a7bb66c41a57.jpg 1800w, /media/ec88db9519a3a47669fd20320e5fe1b318512f2b65293544da1abb0300074564.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>It was a real honor to meet all of you and to document your work. Check out the Inicio in detail at <a href=\"https://www.morralitobikes.com/inicio\" target=\"_blank\">Morralito</a>.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/morralitobikes/\" target=\"_blank\">@MorralitoBikes</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/208f3a9d3cf3840a257e3f48a4256f1e8b17a48101be483a06831ff3033cda49.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b63a7fa8430ea0d3ac53264d570bba8ea1f60ca1a9e88c46ab5a92ae02030c6c.jpg 640w, /media/208f3a9d3cf3840a257e3f48a4256f1e8b17a48101be483a06831ff3033cda49.jpg 1800w, /media/3b146fb7542bdb8972070f181a15a4957d01ae91d110e9fad1d90bab73175d11.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.provacycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Prova</a> Senza Titanium Full Suspension</h3>\n<p>Melbourne, Australia-based Prova is all about incremental design. Mark and Kelly Hester, siblings, will create a new model, ride it, and then improve upon it over the years. Case in point is the Senza mountain bike, which I first documented at the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2024-made-bike-show-part-01#:~:text=Prova%20Cycles%20Prototype%20Full%20Suspension\" target=\"_blank\">2024 Made Bike Show</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f7dd497047e63084c7d453d11c5ccae2c661fec34861d020f11b9be6b1b76c0e.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/d5e9b6e6a891c3f0968bd610293d129fabaf98a19d1fc874c3ebd0e64b89cb02.jpg 640w, /media/f7dd497047e63084c7d453d11c5ccae2c661fec34861d020f11b9be6b1b76c0e.jpg 1800w, /media/ca9c2a8f5bc8d51311c119195e429dd71ad4e7aee9c84fb59a7a980214c51b8e.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>This represents the latest permutation of Prova’s hard work with the Senza. While it still uses the 3V0 suspension layout, Mark has designed Prova’s own swingarm, whereas the first models used the 3Vo-supplied rear end. This has been a slow evolution over the past two years and Mark commented that this new product is so much better and he’s feeling more confident at offering this model as it sits with the new in-house swingarm.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f81f662a617b0c54a34f1715a8e57c953ce5cb1c407f4c7127306d6c05c47c47.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/316f3165582782046486c4e51af6279234d29e83fb9c9f71a96505e834aea92e.jpg 800w, /media/f81f662a617b0c54a34f1715a8e57c953ce5cb1c407f4c7127306d6c05c47c47.jpg 1600w, /media/15f70de84a01aecbd088df57a8089474d99e28e239a8be4c6b260c63800d95ee.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f842479d8aa68332efbdd9da7f60681c792405e7f86ca6850812a5120fb4945b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b43bb3b7dc0c3179d54da4ae15ec892e73485b9ab06c9e71d8de753191378e28.jpg 800w, /media/f842479d8aa68332efbdd9da7f60681c792405e7f86ca6850812a5120fb4945b.jpg 1600w, /media/ff8aa886adc8f364fa4b4b3ed6a5466d8821aca429ad926a6eedcfdc927fa0b2.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e1560ef720eed6b77bb44313e90c8c99f36919cda00ae35771042a863da5573c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/25e9220683d9fa1e04bd1d87e9ac1e55e27d0764788a817f01b5b16f7a8e8122.jpg 800w, /media/e1560ef720eed6b77bb44313e90c8c99f36919cda00ae35771042a863da5573c.jpg 1600w, /media/7dd576dcec8b7a170fa48f81e5633cc83fe69ab246c0c879278806cd6e44f8f6.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>One of the downsides, however, is the time spent welding a Senza. The first prototype only took Mark 40 minutes to build since it relied on an Asia-produced 3Vo CNC aluminum rear end. Now, with the Prova swingarm, the setup and welding time is considerably longer. But Prova’s not about effeciencies, or cutting corners, the team’s one goal is to provide its clients with the best possible product they can offer.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/eeb9f95813c45747988dd437719cf6d4d515a9e80a1ef2322d112187f7cea3ac.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3fcb9b3d48587d513ef5c0529d72f1afe7460a95d96e6d09a234a05adb498da5.jpg 640w, /media/eeb9f95813c45747988dd437719cf6d4d515a9e80a1ef2322d112187f7cea3ac.jpg 1800w, /media/e32add8fa003edf4ba33a734bde49a6bc59713db4e19a46bf2eb87244a632872.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The end result of two years of prototyping is a show-stopper. Well done, Mark and Kelly!</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.provacycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">@ProvaCycles</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/fbfcd07045b0318dfba358eb73e9a97556b7d1c05e10b4a86761fef8cac50575.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ee3edf09eb7debb769e5b9d4693de532043248fd1e4c13669b9b1c8a71c7b19d.jpg 640w, /media/fbfcd07045b0318dfba358eb73e9a97556b7d1c05e10b4a86761fef8cac50575.jpg 1800w, /media/3cbf3442b9d0cd729c9b63ebc12d6a3d2b86c14463ab59300c5a3a59d3a00c2c.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/simworks-doppo-ronin-frame-set-golden-moss\" target=\"_blank\">Sim Works Doppo Ronin</a> with <a href=\"https://sim-works.com/en/news/sunrise-limited-edition-collection\" target=\"_blank\">Sunrise</a> and <a href=\"https://sim-works.com/en/news/47734\" target=\"_blank\">Sunset</a> Parts</h3>\n<p>Nagoya, Japan-based Circles bike shop and its in-house component line Sim Works first launched the Doppo touring bike back in 2016 at NAHBS. Later that year, I was on a bike tour around Japan with <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/makotos-doppo-sim-works-tourer\" target=\"_blank\">Makoto from Sim Works on his Doppo</a>. The brand <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2017-nahbs-sim-works-doppo-touring-bike\" target=\"_blank\">launched future models</a>, refining and repurposing the Doppo name from touring bikes to <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/sim-works-doppo-high-plains-drifter-review\" target=\"_blank\">mountain bikes</a>, adventure bikes, and fendered road bikes, like the one I documented at the <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2026-made-bike-show-picks-05#:~:text=SimWorks%20Doppo%20Wanderer%20Made%20by%20Nitto%20%E2%80%93%20John%20Watson\" target=\"_blank\">2026 Made Bike Show</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5fe5cc46e46e14b5f36943e59aea416e9def38cde84d9b104d653c3816553802.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/77829c975fdc2fa053f82979d88195e1bf5a645be454c750c28ee2873a50d9ca.jpg 800w, /media/5fe5cc46e46e14b5f36943e59aea416e9def38cde84d9b104d653c3816553802.jpg 1600w, /media/a26f960eb43f09614ce2566d30402676956beda61f906630cadf781dd880139a.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/1bdefb0ea2ac56361dab5283354f1d34ad012cea11919b22110172ede3a5a56b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/e712d4b771a48e3403a348b95c05339d022cf0a9e9c9c44031aaa17e655e3495.jpg 800w, /media/1bdefb0ea2ac56361dab5283354f1d34ad012cea11919b22110172ede3a5a56b.jpg 1600w, /media/4485c3754eeb447eb23d5de3736552fddaa51115a4c0cf832892d1193777e557.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d7038489dec6bbbd3cc431784cfbbbded344c7a7f78eba992d2e416019134b84.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0f1819f1dfd229602c9bb0656cc0779c64945b11f451741025146bcb96eb9ff4.jpg 800w, /media/d7038489dec6bbbd3cc431784cfbbbded344c7a7f78eba992d2e416019134b84.jpg 1600w, /media/10da9f7fe8dd93773e065a7c6ef3d496882327bc7936419b4d1639f9e1730d8d.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>At the 2026 Bespoked Osaka show, Sim Works unveiled its latest <a href=\"https://www.sim.works/products/simworks-doppo-ronin-frame-set-golden-moss\" target=\"_blank\">Doppo Ronin model in the Golden Moss</a> colorway. Affixed to the bike were its limited-edition Sunrise edition parts, which include Japan-made Nitto and MKS. <a href=\"https://sim-works.com/en/news/sunrise-limited-edition-collection\" target=\"_blank\">The Sunrise pack</a> includes the Beatnik Seatpost, Tomboy Stemcap, Topcap, SimDrop, and the SimWorks by MKS pedal collection. Reaching across the Pacific to Chico, California, the brand then developed the <a href=\"https://sim-works.com/en/news/47734\" target=\"_blank\">Sunset edition parts</a>. Limited to thirty sets, the Sunset parts include a Paul bottle opener, Short Pull Levers, Klamper disc brakes, and the Motolite V-brakes.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/70dd531942d679cb55538edd00f1a8ac0788d8dbf19eff734a6840c6dee23897.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/4789cad36641aa6f39c1adf5f262c77b354babf8ec5a8585b77a1a13b9714e23.jpg 800w, /media/dcd14241efef103834986b465853db461db75ac460dd5f07899a84a191dbcc59.jpg 1600w, /media/70dd531942d679cb55538edd00f1a8ac0788d8dbf19eff734a6840c6dee23897.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/031f6929e071ccd9d684c7cae49542a9752a56b86cc20eed82a8dd2147bc53e7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/27bfefe2a5b71393cdf9223c4bfb4f635abe8522c1b9f82e4bdd05b57fcfdd2b.jpg 800w, /media/d100a908ce48bd617439ef0d36ca9bbf1637c98f6f105b2fe532e887be03c63e.jpg 1600w, /media/031f6929e071ccd9d684c7cae49542a9752a56b86cc20eed82a8dd2147bc53e7.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The bike, like Masashi, is incredibly stylish and looks amazing on the Golden Moss Doppo Ronin frame.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/circles_jp/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@Circles</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/simworks/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@SimWorks</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/fc76b3d92505ec8c021271e71559151c89ecdf8e867b400402b6f5a9a4a9879c.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/58a68f1b98da6ee6e8a6cdc398853a885779c75c47f27c9985230f79d627d912.jpg 640w, /media/fc76b3d92505ec8c021271e71559151c89ecdf8e867b400402b6f5a9a4a9879c.jpg 1800w, /media/03f36f3a70d415ee5fec6de8609eeba9ac8e3fddee41beb843595f1c4299933c.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.stayercycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stayer Cycles</a> x <a href=\"https://sentient.works/\" target=\"_blank\">Sentient Works</a> x <a href=\"https://www.wizard.works/\" target=\"_blank\">Wizard Works</a> Bike of Friendship</h3>\n<p>London workshop Stayer Cycles debuted what has been referred to as the Bike of Friendship. This mini velo is a 20” full-suspension bike made and styled in collaboration with problem solvers and UK bike makers Sam and Willow from Stayer, Tullen from Sentient Works, Val of <a href=\"http://brompton.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Brompton</a> and <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/blacklinez___/\" target=\"_blank\">Blacklinez</a>, and Harry and Ve of Wizard Works.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a644b2b276fc1b8210aac9307202cc59abb32b24d5eb713c60d4e81f8adc058a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f4ec1f766eac407f61af3409230b60e8fcab0be719dc8bd0c63f4a610522c8c4.jpg 800w, /media/a644b2b276fc1b8210aac9307202cc59abb32b24d5eb713c60d4e81f8adc058a.jpg 1600w, /media/3dd00193996bdd075a9c0b135cbd1638a5ab770f3b400c340a9a8f0048621985.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b3edad6ac9a0200014ba3b02a2f7d85ba291b4fb8efaffb5ca13b785742e01ab.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/73bdd02f1c175d717bef882017dab2bcf855333a8b8affc7bc636cad09ba2dab.jpg 800w, /media/b3edad6ac9a0200014ba3b02a2f7d85ba291b4fb8efaffb5ca13b785742e01ab.jpg 1600w, /media/cefe24c71f2791a1d3713f8b896a08402355ce186232f81816be90efc20bd7a2.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/23e40e6fc65e5e938d0d5dd4d8d20d11e72eff505ad5a4ba30b546adb182fb98.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/41905589f48354eb4e504c8aec2d82718732ce811321e66513f0b1fb1c459751.jpg 800w, /media/23e40e6fc65e5e938d0d5dd4d8d20d11e72eff505ad5a4ba30b546adb182fb98.jpg 1600w, /media/eb1a1ad32f3e7ed6c11958887c049ca6296381f9022d6d39792fc69b9d343ea2.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Mini Velos are great for small apartments or travel. They break down into a smaller bike box, are easier to jetset with, or, in Japan, to rinco on trains. This 20″ BMX trail bike is a collaborative project between Sam from Stayer and Tullen from Sentient, who dressed the frame for the 2026 Bespoked Osaka show in paint by Val and bags from the Wizards. Presented in luggage as a rowdy but prepared travel companion for those looking to shake off the cobwebs after a long haul.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/dec00a274dbee2455cd429e55773369c9d1af6d1a34a34c72cbfd5a5115f414f.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/739e60ab8803ac271da17b4c7335afbc888bde7126a25dc9052eca7008f1fd6d.jpg 640w, /media/dec00a274dbee2455cd429e55773369c9d1af6d1a34a34c72cbfd5a5115f414f.jpg 1800w, /media/3ea5017bfe3990bffa7d914ad4f23f2561924570f6139683f899f59a196ffaaa.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The idea was rooted in asking a single question: how much fun would a full suspension BMX be? From concept to reality, the Bike of Friendship was made possible by many hands, with a special thanks to <a href=\"https://www.hopetech.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hope</a>, <a href=\"https://manitou.hayesbicycle.com/en-gb/\" target=\"_blank\">Manitou</a>, <a href=\"http://brompton.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Brompton</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.schwalbe.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Schwalbe</a>. Val from Brompton and Vee from Wizard Works developed a flame-adorned <a href=\"https://www.wizard.works/product-category/bags/brompton-bags/\" target=\"_blank\">Leyline Brompton Bag</a>, and Stayer integrated the Brompton Carrier Block system to the headtube for ease of removal.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/34f80967629ba985ccb9586d1944eec73f2e5936136dcc7c67ba316216245366.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/72dbcd956e04598cfa376afeb01a1980903738385d66dbd74c76ce43eb11ad3a.jpg 640w, /media/34f80967629ba985ccb9586d1944eec73f2e5936136dcc7c67ba316216245366.jpg 1800w, /media/29abacb2cf60b4e807bc7783e972b06508bf9ac598887bb4a525667a06e62bcf.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Many thanks to Judith from Stayer for the hangs and for bringing the stoke all the way from the UK.</p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stayercycles/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@Stayer</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/sentient.works/\" target=\"_blank\">@SentientWorks</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/wizard.works/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@WizardWorks</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5b812e76f74e2ec63acd4b222bcb07f5177fa68ad03076aa0598826bccff39d4.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0f4a3ddf667eaa268fe30d1a0d901c6464ce53c80ba0c0af5be01c999aa7b418.jpg 640w, /media/5b812e76f74e2ec63acd4b222bcb07f5177fa68ad03076aa0598826bccff39d4.jpg 1800w, /media/82e23e75fc0c22267d8df6f7f684fca1de991ac39de5387bfa57c22a5ed5b8e9.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.stayercycles.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stayer Cycles</a> x <a href=\"https://www.babyldn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Babyldn</a></h3>\n<p>Speaking of Stayer, the London-based builders made a travel mini velo for Marlon Plein of BabyLdn. In hopes of making the bike lighter and stiffer in the rear, Sam from Stayer welded up the chain and seat stays from aluminum, which are then bolted to the front triangle of the bike via clevises.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/dc57c0b3b00a397de8e015fb4c4b689ec705088b255e97e74443de7d922dd57d.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ed62b919d85c2353876f13ec863d4cd36a1456561efa22a5cc6edd28163f2e64.jpg 800w, /media/dc57c0b3b00a397de8e015fb4c4b689ec705088b255e97e74443de7d922dd57d.jpg 1600w, /media/a5c3a45234b984387c51dc092c471d1eb1a3e13e45acd6b3f7daabd21aff3c68.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e5a71813942676a3006358885b5f94f863202c97ca39e6d79f918955a59b3316.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0f42cab6d8cce0094d3e887c17b48ced17aa1d249098af8bd5cb20a64ede6d43.jpg 800w, /media/e5a71813942676a3006358885b5f94f863202c97ca39e6d79f918955a59b3316.jpg 1600w, /media/7329afd30b4190252ebaa8b61ca4ee767021b1d868523287e734be87265e1051.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/63cf3e4aeb9770fd1510c9eb374b43367f017666192d398e159eb15a41ee38f2.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/3547e43ca9d6edc2eae5d4d63d0b5665b74aba510a93083b7a6bd07be8cdb873.jpg 800w, /media/63cf3e4aeb9770fd1510c9eb374b43367f017666192d398e159eb15a41ee38f2.jpg 1600w, /media/7b167bc0a4aec3cbae0a2538a992bafad0870bff02ef1f1b9c4403911240b850.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>The frame’s truss fork features a unique cable stop integrated into its brace to allow for consistent modulation and control for the cantilever brakes. Marlon’s bike was made possible with parts from <a href=\"https://www.mkspedal.com/?q=ja\" target=\"_blank\">MKS</a>, <a href=\"https://www.paulcomp.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul Component</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.whiteind.com/\" target=\"_blank\">White Industries</a>.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/4fd85b74717128d7129f7450e410b88ab9ed3022fc85bd71065208fe2eb0beba.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/250361768ee1d05a69b2c19598374ad78688d598cfce431869ab642988bb889e.jpg 640w, /media/4fd85b74717128d7129f7450e410b88ab9ed3022fc85bd71065208fe2eb0beba.jpg 1800w, /media/45391781cb260dbd6dc5b24b841cd9e30f219ab2c290b50970533d9b61981e03.jpg\" /></p>\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/stayercycles/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@Stayer</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/babyldn.bikes/?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\">@BabyLdn</a></h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/f9fd5eea3c0bbb108d8df7a5414991806d8c0427188ae9a2c2b7679de681aeb5.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/9954310137f6738ee011aefc3c7c315dab21a4b533d1f5b27859b3e5032d4c21.jpg 640w, /media/f9fd5eea3c0bbb108d8df7a5414991806d8c0427188ae9a2c2b7679de681aeb5.jpg 1800w, /media/21b9972d77bdd0aa14d9f6047ffd04feaefb08e2579ae6221c6854d95f0e7f58.jpg\" /></p>\n<p><strong>The Radavist thanks <a href=\"https://circles-jp.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Circles Japan</a> for sponsoring our 2026 Bespoked Osaka coverage and our independent Reportage!</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-05\">2026 Bespoked Osaka Picks 04: Crumbworks, Morralito, Prova, Sim Works, Stayer</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"John Watson","comments":"https://theradavist.com/2026-bespoked-osaka-picks-05#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"9b258b8f73cb73fd5d612b72167fb960f401aa21d81bdf64c49b13775ec9b6df","category":"Cycling"}